      "id": "cdksjj8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6.1 Primary Memory (Main Memory)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Primary memory (Main Memory) directly interacts with the CPU and includes volatile RAM and non-volatile ROM.",
        "RAM (Random Access Memory) provides temporary high-speed access for active programs, losing data when power is off.",
        "ROM (Read Only Memory) holds permanent firmware instructions like BIOS required during the system startup process.",
        "Cache memory acts as a high-speed semiconductor buffer between the CPU and main memory to accelerate processing.",
        "Secondary memory devices (HDDs, SSDs, optical drives) provide non-volatile, mass storage capacity for long-term data preservation.",
        "Memory measurement follows a hierarchy: 1 Nibble = 4 Bits, 1 Byte = 8 Bits, 1 KB = 1024 Bytes, progressing up to TB and beyond."
      ],
      "id": "6azk5ca"
    },
